flowchart TD

    A[Method Call Occurs] --> B[Check All Aspects' Pointcuts]

    B -->|No Match| R[No AOP Interception; Execute Method Normally] --> S[Return Result to Caller]
B -->|Match Found| C[Create JoinPoint captures current call context]

%% If a match is found, we evaluate which advice is applicable

C --> D{Around Advice Present?}

%% Around Advice wraps the method call
D -->|Yes| E[Execute 'around' Advice Method Call Inside]
D -->|No| F[No 'around' Advice]

%% If no around advice, we can have 'before' advice
F --> G{Before Advice Present?}
G -->|Yes| H[Execute 'before' Advice]
G -->|No| I[Skip 'before' Advice]

%% After before advice or if none is present, call original method
E --> J[Call Original Method Inside 'around' Advice]
I --> K[Call Original Method Directly]

%% After calling the method, two paths: success or exception
%% For simplicity, we show them as separate flows

%% If called from around advice:
J -->|Method Returns Normally| L[Execute 'after returning' Advice if any]
J -->|Method Throws Exception| M[Execute 'after throwing' Advice if an]

%% If called without around advice:
K -->|Method Returns Normally| N[Execute 'after returning' Advice if any]
K -->|Method Throws Exception| O[Execute 'after throwing' Advice if any]

%% After returning or throwing advice, 'after' advice always runs (if present)
L --> P[Execute 'after' Advice if any] --> Q[Return Final Result]
M --> P[Execute 'after' Advice if any] --> Q[Exception Propagates or Handled]
N --> P[Execute 'after' Advice if any] --> Q[Return Final Result]
O --> P[Execute 'after' Advice if any] --> Q[Exception Propagates or Handled]

%% If using around advice, after completing method execution inside it,
%% control returns to around advice which then returns final result
E -->|After Inner Method and advices| Q

%% Final step
Q[Final Output to Caller]
